% A pattern that arrives in a variable is compiled when the call runs, over
% the binding that supplies it, so one that is not a regular expression is
% an evaluation error rather than a check error: the evaluation stops,
% nothing is derived, and the error names the rule and why.  The good
% pattern is met first and does not save the rule.
name("main.c").
pattern("\\.c$"). pattern("a(").

hit(N, P) :- name(N), pattern(P), match(N, P) >= 0.
hit(N, P)?
